/****************************
Change record (most recent last). Each entry: date, branch, summary, rules concerned.

14-15 Nov 2026, branch trigger-fqn-naming (Fang)
Trigger channels are named with the fully qualified name of their node container:
<e>_<FQN of the container>__in instead of <e>__in (operation triggerChan).
Generator convention, not a rule of the manual: the manual (Rules 42, 43, 55) writes the event
eventId(e).id(source) and does not say how the channel is declared; RoboTool's CSP-M names the channel e__
and declares it in the module of each container. In one Isabelle theory the path of the container has to
be part of the name.
The event channels <e>_in / <e>_out are deliberately not qualified (connections match them by name).
Rules concerned: channel declarations (createchanParaNC, not covered by the manual), Rule 41 (tidsR and
transSync, through tevent_str), Rule 42 (renameTriggerEventsPairL), Rule 43 (tevent_str, tevent),
Rule 55 (trigger).
Templates (circusM2T_HOLCSP.egl, circusM2T_HOLCSP_trans_core.egl): the paragraphs of a node are selected by
exact match instead of contains(nd); eventBase() finds the event of a trigger channel from the declaration
of the channel; NID_name removed, the type of Trans is printed from its parameter declaration.

15 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Composite states. Implemented as RoboTool's CSP-M writes them (CSP generator 3.1.0.202608041330; read from
the CSP-M of the test models c1 to c6 and of Adaptation_Plan), where this differs from the manual it is
said at the rule.
Rule 52 (composeNodes): the composite node is added to the composition.
Rule 60 (createCompositeStateAsActionParas): Behaviour (Rule 40 with the state as node container, During,
the two-sided write synchronisation over all variables of the machine, hiding of enteredSS and terminate),
During, RunEntered; the interrupt of the state instead of the interrupt of its container. Checked against
Rule 60 of the manual: four differences, all following the CSP-M, listed at the rule.
Channel declarations (createchanParaNC, not covered by the manual): split into the part of a node container
and the part of the machine. Generator convention.
Rules 47, 49, 50 (vars; called through Rule 48 for a composite state, never reached before): three
corrections (result set not instantiated; guard of a transition; left-hand side of an indexed assignment).
Templates: paragraphs printed container by container, innermost first; interleaving as |||; Trans core:
lemma names with the container when there are several.

15 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Rule 45 (usedVariables of an expression; usedVariablesInExpr, usedVariablesInExprModel): a LetExpression is
treated explicitly, the variables of the values of its declarations and of its body (generator issue X).
Before, a variable occurring only in the value of a let was not read before the action (Rule 62, readState)
and was free in the generated equation. Changes the output of models with let (flat MakePlan).

15 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
User-defined types of imported packages (generator issue W; completes issue C, 25e7662): createTypeDeclPara
translates the types of the selected file's package and the types of other non-toolkit packages reachable
from the selected file (typeDeclsToTranslate), dependencies first. Names are not qualified; a clash of two
type names stops the generation with an error. Changes the output of models that use types of an imported
package (dti/enriched: Legitimate, Adaptation_Plan).

15 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Tuple selection (generator issue Y): createTupleSelExprGeneral sets the new optional attribute arity of
TupleSelExpr (circus_metamodel.ecore; a deviation from CZT, marked there by an annotation) to the number of
components of the RoboChart product type. The templates print the projection of an n-tuple from it
(tupleSelection.eol); before, component 2 was always printed as snd, which is wrong for n > 2.

16 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Toolkit functions (generator issue AA). The manual has no rule for them (Chapter 4 Rule 45 omits usedVariables
of expressions; Appendix D, pp. 167-171 of the August 2022 PDF, shows the four toolkits, the sequence toolkit
on p. 171, but no translation; corrected 17 Nov 2026, this comment said that Appendix D lacks the sequence
toolkit). createCallExpr writes a call of a
function of a toolkit with its qualified name <package>_<function> (toolkitCallName), as RoboTool's CSP-M
generator; the templates print it by toolkitFunctions.eol (imported here as well). Supported: the sequence and
set toolkits except range, iter, squash, extract; size for sequences only. Any other toolkit function stops
the generation with an error naming it. Preconditions: an assignment, a call, a communication and an if
statement are guarded by the preconditions of the toolkit functions they call (toolkitGuards,
withToolkitGuards in createStmtAsAction), placed and collected as in the CSP-M generator
(CStatementGenerator.xtend, robochart-csp-gen a6412b40c8); the guards for division and indexing of the
CSP-M generator are not generated.

16 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Rule 60 (Behaviour): machineVarNames follows allVariables(stm) of the CSP-M generator: also the parameters of
an operation definition and the variables of provided interfaces (empty for every model the RoboChart
validator accepts). No change for state machines.

16 Nov 2026, branch m2t-partial-output (Fang)
Markers instead of stopping (generatorErrors.eol, imported here and by the templates). An unsupported toolkit
function and size of a set (toolkitCallName) are written as calls of GENERATOR_ERROR_unsupported_toolkit_
<package>_<function> and GENERATOR_ERROR_size_of_set, a missing pre_ entry (toolkitGuardsOf) as the guard
GENERATOR_ERROR_no_precondition_guard_<function>; before, each stopped the generation. Isabelle stops at the
command containing the marker. The type name clash of issue W still stops the generation here (M2M): a
declaration under a marker name would be a valid declaration, and every reference to the type is printed by
its unqualified name, so no marker can make Isabelle stop at the right place (generator CLAUDE.md, "M2T
errors and output").

16 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang); check REMOVED 23 Nov 2026
Exit actions of inner states and input triggers: from 16 to 23 Nov 2026 a check exitTriggerConflicts (at
Rule 60) warned when an exit action of an inner state (any depth) of a composite state read or wrote the
variable bound by the input trigger of a transition leaving it. Removed on 23 Nov 2026 (Fang): RoboTool's
CSP-M has the same unordered structure (CTransitionGenerator compileTransition/compileTriggerForMemory,
CStateGenerator Node_rule and tidsR) and RoboTool gives no hint (validator, CSP generator); it is a known
problem of the semantics itself (Pedro, 16 Nov 2026), no longer reported. The warning mechanism
(generatorNote) stays; GG uses it. Comments at Rules 41 and 60: Pedro's explanations of 16 Nov 2026
(docs/SEMANTICS_DIFFERENCES.md, entry 6).

16 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Rule 60 (Behaviour): machineVarNames also takes the variables of the required interfaces (rInterfaces), as
allVariables of the CSP-M generator (generator issue EE). No change for the models generated so far.

22 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Preconditions of user-defined functions (generator issue CC; createAssignmentStmtAsAction, Rule 66;
userPreconditionGuard, substitutedPrecondition). For x = f(args) with f user-defined, the guard is the
conjunction of the preconditions of f with the arguments in place of the formal parameters (by position, on a
copy; bound names of the precondition that occur in an argument renamed first). Toolkit functions are skipped
there (AA guards them). A precondition that createExpr cannot translate (quantifiers) is printed as the guard
GENERATOR_ERROR_untranslated_precondition_<f>. Before, the preconditions were copied with the formal parameters,
also for toolkit functions (second guard besides AA). The guards are provisional (decision of Fang, 22 Nov
2026, for the release of composite-states): as the CSP-M; the manual does not treat preconditions as guards
(Ana and Alvaro, January 2026); removed when preconditions become definedness proof obligations. Changes the
output of models with x = f(args) for a function with preconditions (toy models d1, d2; test model c9).

22 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Three issues present since the rules of the ITP 2026 paper or since 9 Oct 2026 (docs/COMPOSITE_RELEASE_TEST.md,
Sections 11 and 13). FF: Rule 50 (vars of an if statement) no longer calls vars on a missing else (stack
overflow for an if without else in a state action); Rule 68 (createIfStmtAsAction) gives an if without else the
else branch Skip, as the CSP-M (before, "if b then P" without else, not parsed by Isabelle); the templates print
" else " with spaces. GG: createFunctionDefsAsAxParas also declares the functions of imported packages that the
model calls, transitively through the pre- and postconditions of the functions called (importedFunctionsToTranslate;
toolkits excluded), with a warning on a name clash. II: the parameter type of a function with three or more
parameters is one n-ary product (A x B x C), matching the flat tuple of a call; before, nested pairs ((A x B) x C)
(printed so since 9faa957). Changes the output of models with an if without else, with calls of functions of
imported packages, and with functions of three or more parameters.

23 Nov 2026, branch composite-states (Fang)
Records, enumerations and names (generator issues KK, LL, MM, NN; all four also on main 2976313;
docs/COMPOSITE_RELEASE_TEST.md Section 15, docs/SEMANTICS_DIFFERENCES.md entries 10 and 19). KK: defaultValueAsZExpr
gives the defaults of RoboTool's CSP-M (first literal of an enumeration, record of the field defaults, '''' for
string, constant function for a function type, markers for unsupported types) instead of 0. LL: createExpr
translates field access r.f (Selection) to (R.f r) and record literals to \<lparr>R.f = e, ...\<rparr> (_reclit_); an
assignment r.f = e or x[i] = e also reads the root variable and the variables of the indices (usedVariables,
Rule 50 vars, leftReadVariables); field names are qualified by the record in selection, update and literal. MM:
enumeration literals keep their parameters (Branch.expr), a literal with arguments is (L (a) (b)) (_conapp_). NN:
the variables of the generated definitions are x__a, y__a, n__id, value__v, b__a, Q__a, P__a (before x, y, n,
value, b, Q, P, captured by a field, literal or function of that name); the templates print record field and
constructor names quoted (a keyword such as value cannot be written bare) and declare char :: discrete_cpo (string
variables). createTypeExpr gives markers for relation,
vector and matrix types. The exit-action check of composite states (exitTriggerConflicts, 16 Nov 2026) was
removed (entry above). Changes the output of every model (names n__id, value__v, x__a, y__a, b__a, Q__a, P__a),
and of models with records, enumerations with parameters, uninitialised variables of enumeration, record or
string type, and indexed or field assignments.
******************************/


/****************************
rct Vs EMF (1)
when using rct as source model, if the source is set as both read on load and store on disposal, the model is deleted every time the program run
this issue is avoided when use exported EMF models
One thing to notice:
when change in rct directly, after create local vars for the shared vars, as long as the required interface in stm is deleted, all the vars in statement point to the local declared vars automatically.
But when do EOL transformation, it is not the case.
Even if we delete all stm.rinterfaces, the vars in statements still point to the interfaces.
So we need to replace all the vars expr by expr with the one in the allLocalVariables.

This is a tedious process, but can not be avoided.
We will need the usedVariablesModel again and modify it to implement the FQN replacement.

30.06.2024
******************************/


/****************************
rct Vs EMF (2)
using EMF exported rct as source model does not support functions in Z toolkit, e.g., size()
using rct as source model supports Z toolkit functions
